#     transcript.partial            — speculative fast-model hypothesis; MUTABLE, may be followed
#                                     by transcript.retract; NEVER pipe to the LLM
#     transcript.delta              — append-only COMMITTED text; pipe deltas or utterance_end.text
#                                     to the LLM, nothing else
#     utterance_end                 — explicit conversational end-of-turn, distinct from VAD
#                                     segmentation; {utterance_id, reason: endpoint|timeout|
#                                     max_len|session_end, text}; THE hand-off trigger to the LLM
# - Timing assumptions: endpoint = ~300 ms min-silence + max backstop (v1 ask, semantic
#   endpointing later); partial latency well under 400 ms from speech onset; ts is seconds,
#   monotone per run; seq strictly increases per line.
#
# Scenario: one clean question, no hesitations. Orchestrator expectation: cancel any in-flight ftts
# playback on speech_started (barge-in), wait for utterance_end, hand text to the LLM.
